    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d589">

                <pb facs="1426" n="1410" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.31/9–1751: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >GATT</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">Delegation to the Secretary of State
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d589-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-09-17T20:00:00+01:00">September 17,
                            1951—8 p. m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Tagg 7. At plenary GATT session today<anchor n="2" xml:id="d589-f2"/> Czech
                    delegate reserved right place two additional items on agenda if diplomatic
                    representations in Wash do not bring satisfactory replies. First complaint
                    related to general US action in refusing all export licenses for export to
                    Czech. Second item refers to refusal of specific export licenses for Czech goods
                    sent to US and rejected by US customers. Czech seek to have these goods returned
                    to Czech. Claim some of these latter goods not permitted be re-exported.</p>
                <p>Pls send soonest available background and what steps will be taken.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept Tagg 7, rptd info Praha 1.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d589-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d589-f1-content">
                <p>For the composition of the U.S. Delegation to the Sixth Session of the
                    Contracting Parties of the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade which convened
                    at Geneva on September 17, 1951, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, October 1, 1951, p. 553. The Delegation Chairman was Willard
                    L. Thorp, Assistant Secretary of State for Economic Affairs, and the Vice
                    Chairman was John M. Leddy, Acting Director, Office of Economic Defense and
                    Trade Policy. Files of the U.S. Delegation are in the GATT Files, Lot 63 D 134,
                    Box 268 (FRC Accession 65A987) and Lot 66 D 209, Box 454 (FRC Accession
                    71A6682).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d589-f2" n="2" xml:id="d589-f2-content">
                <p>The Summary Records of the Sixth Session are in GATT Files, Lot 63 D 134, Box
                    268. There were 27 plenary meetings, September 17–October 27, 1951.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
